    "summary": "The round-1 fixes I checked are in place. The student query selects source_table. The v3 producer is off by default and assignWork blocks it before any write. The protected source_id grant is parsed from the database row, and metadata can't widen it. Old explicit assignment context is authoritative and doesn't fall back to another grant. Scoped v3 staged and indicator caches don't read legacy keys. Unless deadline locks are strict. One preallocated row ID flows into source_id, metadata, the notification and the returned route. Two medium defects remain in the v3 progress adapter. (1) An explicit Resume and revise drops a credited Completed-earlier step back to started. (2) Records saved under step IDs outside the registry, such as the indicator flashcard decks, are written with the v3 prefix but never read back. Two lower-severity regressions also need fixing: old-edition signed-in renders now use different device keys, and Chapter 1 copy changed while it is still labeled as the frozen main revision.",
