        "path": "src/bootcamps/conditionals/courseProgress.tsx",
        "evidence": "createEditionCourseStore.resume writes saveRaw(`${prefix}${id}`, {...previous, ..., reopen: true, status: 'started'}). A prefixed record now exists, so the projection is skipped and visible[id] becomes status 'started'. A student whose earlier Chapter 1 completion was counting toward v3 (CourseTracker and CourseContinue read visible) loses that credit just by clicking 'Resume and revise'. For drills like SourceWorksheetDrill and StagedReasoningDrill, the copied state is already complete, but nothing re-records 'done' until another answer event happens. This contradicts the screen copy ('Your completed work from the earlier course counts here') and the finished-code contract ('Ordinary answer edits after completion retain completed course credit'). The OpeningCourse test only checks that resume is called, not the resulting status.",
        "fix": "On resume, write the prefixed snapshot with status 'done' (no reopen), keeping done/total and sourceCompletion. Reopen only when the registry contentRevision differs, as FullCourseDrill already does with signatures. Add a test: projected done -> resume -> visible status still done and tracker percentage unchanged."
      },
      {
        "id": "R2-2",
        "severity": "medium",
        "path": "src/bootcamps/conditionals/courseProgress.tsx",
        "evidence": "In v3, save() writes every stepId to `full-conditionals-v3:<id>`, but `visible` is filled only by looping over registry `steps`. IndicatorWordDeck records under INDICATOR_DECK_STEP 'flashcards-indicators' and 'flashcards-indicators-group-1/2', which aren't registry steps. useCourseStep then reads store.steps[stepId] as undefined, so the account copy is never restored in v3. Only the scoped device cache resumes these decks. Another device, or a cleared cache, starts a new round even though the account holds the work. The same applies to any other non-registry step ID recorded under the v3 provider.",
        "fix": "In createEditionCourseStore, copy every raw key that starts with the v3 prefix into visible under its unprefixed ID. Limit projection to registry steps. Add a test that renders IndicatorWordDeck under the v3 edition store with only an account record (no device bytes) and confirms it resumes."
