        "evidence": "For the old edition, routes.tsx passes storageScope=editionStorageScope(userId, undefined)=userId. CourseBody now forwards `storageScope ?? progress?.storageScope` to OpeningCourseContent, which passes it to StagedReasoningDrill. FlashcardTools also receives it. Previously both got no scope. Old-edition keys therefore move from `conditional-staged-v1:<mode>` and `conditional-indicator-words-v1[-group-n]` to `...:<userId>...`. Device-only drafts that were never saved to the account no longer load in the unchanged old course. The plan says 'Old renders retain old scopes/keys.' The new tests cover v3 isolation but not this legacy path.",
